<ecoSpold xmlns="http://www.EcoInvent.org/EcoSpold02">
  <activityDataset>
    <activityDescription>
      <activity id="dc42b3b1-d56c-5997-bd66-0515d8d4f1af" activityNameId="a9d4c2b7-95b8-5816-aa38-4d0015b9ffaa" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Uranium enrichment centrifuge plant</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Uranium enrichment centrifuge plant
The material and energy requirements for construction have been roughly estimated on the basis of the data from an old US reference and scaling them down by the ratio of the capacities (centrifuge process is modular, therefore in first approximation linearity can be assumed for requirements). It is assumed that 75% of reinforced concrete is dumped as non-contaminated waste from decommissioning. Although Russian facilities have higher capacity, the original dataset developed for URENCO plants has been directly used herewith for the previously explained reason, with the only difference of electricity requirements from the Russian mix. This mix has been approximated using existing ecoinvent v2.0 electricity datasets for Europe.;
UUID: eb105de6-e14c-3e73-9ff0-99f67a383c0b
The module includes: estimated land use of a plant with capacity of 1500 t SWU (separative work unit); energy (electricity, diesel, and light oil) and material requirements for the construction of the facility; transport requirements during construction; energy and transport requirements (for non-contaminated inerts concrete with reinforcing bars) during decommissioning; disposal of the non-contaminated inerts. The non contaminated metals are assumed to be recycled.
Location: &lt;null&gt;
Technology: Available construction material and energy data refer to a model plant in early 1980s.
Time period: undefined
Production volume: na
Sampling: Literature 
Extrapolations: none
Uncertainty adjustments: none
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_eb105de6-e14c-3e73-9ff0-99f67a383c0b.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
